{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791741913,"nonce":"ZxGPpNnrBdfzftwVaZo9xM8uMGo=","title":"Ashui's two-frame CSS list snapshot renders neighboring text in the wrong card under Ash hybrid mode. Interpreter mode renders the same scene correctly. The root cause is not yet isolated.","message":"Reproducer source (committed):\nhttps://github.com/rayzor-blade/ashui/blob/fdac296763e170dcadd7d829669696b89124ed04/tools/snapshot/scenes/CssLists.hx\n\nFrom that Ashui checkout, with its native dependencies built/staged:\n\n```sh\ntools/snapshot/run.sh tools/snapshot/scenes/CssLists.hx\n\nASH_MODE=interp \\\nASHUI_SNAPSHOT_DIR=\"$PWD/.ashui/snapshots/css-lists-interp\" \\\ntools/snapshot/run.sh tools/snapshot/scenes/CssLists.hx\n```\n\nThe default snapshot run uses hybrid mode with the application preset. Frame 0 uses lower-roman markers in the left ordered list and square/circle markers in the right unordered list. Frame 1 replaces the stylesheet: left markers become decimal-leading-zero, and right markers become none.\n\nExpected: both frames retain each list's text; frame 1 has left markers 03., 04., 08. and no right markers/gutter.\n\nObserved: hybrid frame 0 is correct. Hybrid frame 1 keeps the correct left numbers but substitutes the neighboring right card's strings into the left card. Instead of \"Review the changes\", \"Capture dark and light snapshots\", and \"Publish the package\", it can render \"Inspect each theme\", \"Check compact layouts\", and \"Verify pointer feedback\" there. Both interpreter frames are correct.\n\nHaxe Text.text() tracing on frame 1 still reports the original left strings at their correct left-card bounds (x=81, y=244/266/288). The right strings retain right-card bounds (x=453). The generated text Piece signals also retain the correct values. This narrows the discrepancy to later processing, but native retained text/display buffers have not yet been inspected.\n\nHybrid --jit-log summary:\n```text\n[tiered] attempted=177 succeeded=129 failed=0 compiled_calls=80134 fallbacks=0 cranelift=176 llvm=0\n```\n\nLLVM was not involved in this run. No culprit function has been isolated; possibilities include promoted code, native-call arguments/buffers, or renderer state. This report does not yet establish a JIT miscompile.\n\nEvidence retained locally in the Ashui checkout:\n- .ashui/snapshots/css-lists-000.png (hybrid, correct)\n- .ashui/snapshots/css-lists-001.png (hybrid, wrong)\n- .ashui/snapshots/css-lists-interp/css-lists-001.png (interpreter, correct)\n- .ashui/snapshots/css-lists-trace.log\n- .ashui/snapshots/css-lists-jit.log\n\nInitial downstream report: rayzor-blade/ashui git-bug fee30f1. Native ABI dependency at that Ashui commit is project-blinc/blinc_abi 052e685a15563dab147acdba7126ed016fe66e80. Tested on local macOS with ash/target/release/ash; the binary's build revision was not captured during the original comparison.\n\nAcceptance: isolate the first interp/hybrid divergence, add a minimal regression in Ash if the defect is there, and verify both CssLists frames retain their correct text in hybrid mode.","files":null}]}